def is_leap(y):
    if y % 4 != 0:
        return False
    else:
        if y % 100 != 0:
            return True
        else:
            if y % 400 == 0:
                return True
            else:
                return False

TESTING: an exception inside an exception. Banning and/or is what forces them to
see the shape instead of copying a one-liner.

MARK WRONG IF:
- 1900 comes back True. That is the entire point — divides by 4, but is a century
  year that does not divide by 400.
- 2000 comes back False. They stopped at the century rule.
- They used and/or anyway. Logic may be right; the exercise was the nesting.
  Your call on partial credit.

CHECK: 1900 and 2000. Nearly every wrong answer fails one of them.

